{"lines":[{"y":0.047965116461507584,"c":1,"h":0.014571756458563789,"t":"Test 2","w":0.061601645151774076,"x":0.092402462746190683},{"w":0.31006159464518229,"h":0.014594909645463172,"x":0.092402467461803084,"c":1,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","y":0.095870206419374826},{"y":0.13215339256354364,"w":0.82751541137695317,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","h":0.017699115044247815,"x":0.092402458470997623,"c":1},{"t":"Passage 2 below.","y":0.14956676311617789,"w":0.17111254374186197,"h":0.018846537159607379,"x":0.092048832508218603,"c":1},{"t":"Athletes and stress","w":0.28167976379394527,"h":0.021469998430010073,"c":1,"x":0.37148566786277853,"y":0.19373765412599264},{"c":1,"h":0.019355761547707573,"t":"A It isn't easy being a professional athlete. Not only are the physical demands greater","x":0.090289639640906597,"y":0.22644682152465689,"w":0.83584843953450516},{"h":0.017487308761011566,"x":0.13552360655622417,"t":"than most people could handle, athletes also face intense psychological pressure","c":1,"w":0.77002054850260426,"y":0.24563953490633061},{"h":0.018790817260742276,"c":1,"y":0.26293347544635015,"t":"during competition. This is something that British tennis player Emma Raducanu","w":0.7578029886881511,"x":0.13752784754993019},{"h":0.019062949211548275,"t":"wrote about on social media following her withdrawal from the 2021 Wimbledon","y":0.28000901635745556,"c":1,"x":0.13751099192502911,"w":0.74963124593098962},{"c":1,"w":0.77207392374674466,"h":0.015996947049391363,"y":0.29941002957230267,"x":0.13552361291977008,"t":"tournament. Though the young player had been doing well in the tournament, she"},{"y":0.31681415923660938,"t":"began having difficulty regulating her breathing and heart rate during a match,","h":0.01894165421657501,"c":1,"w":0.73716634114583335,"x":0.13757699360988851},{"y":0.33421828917178797,"h":0.017525896843204158,"t":"which she later attributed to 'the accumulation of the excitement and the buzz'.","c":1,"x":0.13757701298507971,"w":0.74332646687825532},{"w":0.78850102742513029,"y":0.36191860467433523,"h":0.017441860412777621,"c":1,"t":"For athletes, some level of performance stress is almost unavoidable. But there are","x":0.13347022537378297},{"t":"many different factors that dictate just how people's minds and bodies respond to","c":1,"x":0.13757700899088879,"y":0.37935103231321288,"w":0.76591374715169269,"h":0.01745129306759452},{"y":0.39823008839775342,"t":"stressful events. Typically, stress is the result of an exchange between two factors:","w":0.77823410034179685,"x":0.13757699484156868,"h":0.017467585988452772,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.76180699666341156,"y":0.41710914440968705,"t":"demands and resources. An athlete may feel stressed about an event if they feel","h":0.016030390354032753,"x":0.1375769943747403},{"h":0.019036433127074037,"y":0.43299837890234505,"t":"the demands on them are greater than they can handle. These demands include","x":0.13545291956969549,"w":0.75989573160807289,"c":1},{"h":0.019012828140483884,"x":0.13757699305079862,"y":0.45191740391715873,"t":"the high level of physical and mental effort required to succeed, and also the","w":0.72073923746744795,"c":1},{"x":0.1375770012733894,"t":"athlete's concerns about the difficulty of the event, their chance of succeeding, and","y":0.46947674467927669,"w":0.78028747558593747,"h":0.019018830380960194,"c":1},{"h":0.018981099761692821,"y":0.48691860514434182,"x":0.13757699496020251,"t":"any potential dangers such as injury. Resources, on the other hand, are a person's","w":0.77823410034179696,"c":1},{"t":"ability to cope with these demands. These include factors such as the competitor's","y":0.50432436238436762,"w":0.77627660115559904,"h":0.018867165219467297,"x":0.1375317120104205,"c":1},{"t":"degree of confidence, how much they believe they can control the situation's","x":0.13752884094660089,"y":0.52175975160237809,"h":0.019368374804831556,"c":1,"w":0.72289052327473957},{"h":0.017441860412777732,"c":1,"t":"outcome, and whether they're looking forward to the event or not.","x":0.13757700235551493,"y":0.5406976744321349,"w":0.61806981404622396},{"x":0.13757700741988202,"y":0.5683139536026276,"w":0.7741272989908855,"h":0.016051828052441985,"c":1,"t":"Each new demand or change in circumstances affects whether a person responds"},{"h":0.019802599881602601,"c":1,"y":0.58566776512271945,"w":0.77424758911132807,"t":"positively or negatively to stress. Typically, the more resources a person feels they","x":0.13751838127548296},{"c":1,"w":0.78644765218098955,"h":0.015997804512316471,"t":"have in handling the situation, the more positive their stress response. This positive","y":0.60465116290610832,"x":0.13552360705934216},{"c":1,"y":0.62209302336900762,"t":"stress response is called a challenge state. But should the person feel there are too","x":0.13552361346138619,"w":0.78850102742513017,"h":0.015988371857499573},{"h":0.01861608162038797,"t":"many demands placed on them, the more likely they are to experience a negative","x":0.13547629701289338,"y":0.63937984116033664,"c":1,"w":0.77012395222981778},{"x":0.13552361834603158,"w":0.74127309163411459,"c":1,"y":0.65840707948657951,"t":"stress response - known as a threat state. Research shows that the challenge","h":0.016011525044399066},{"x":0.13757701333499833,"y":0.67581120923960958,"t":"states lead to good performance, while threat states lead to poorer performance.","w":0.75975357055664072,"h":0.017502744218944377,"c":1},{"t":"So, in Emma Raducanu's case, a much larger audience, higher expectations and","c":1,"w":0.76386037190755207,"x":0.13757700080187077,"y":0.69321533908675026,"h":0.017540474838211861},{"x":0.13544439953446707,"w":0.73320810953776039,"h":0.017984722216220717,"c":1,"t":"facing a more skilful opponent, may all have led her to feel there were greater","y":0.71065403676545613},{"h":0.016071550825000891,"w":0.78028747558593747,"y":0.72965116290563459,"c":1,"x":0.13552361319998588,"t":"demands being placed on her at Wimbledon - but she didn't have the resources to"},{"x":0.13347022470066824,"t":"tackle them. This led to her experiencing a threat response.","w":0.56878850301106765,"y":0.74709302336848393,"h":0.016033820205733407,"c":1},{"h":0.016066406047449688,"w":0.76796712239583331,"x":0.13347023740649072,"t":"Our challenge and threat responses essentially influence how our body responds","y":0.77463126824993245,"c":1},{"w":0.74743326822916667,"c":1,"h":0.017699115044247704,"y":0.79203539799979295,"x":0.13552361202930191,"t":"to stressful situations, as both affect the production of adrenaline and cortisol -"},{"h":0.022354382540272333,"c":1,"w":0.76000442504882804,"t":"also known as 'stress hormones'. During a challenge state, adrenaline increases","y":0.80729644042124926,"x":0.13541254313133824},{"x":0.13543610055992492,"c":1,"y":0.827198350059417,"w":0.77634546915690106,"h":0.018924463322732232,"t":"the amount of blood pumped from the heart and expands the blood vessels, which"},{"y":0.8459302325818171,"h":0.01749159607563755,"c":1,"x":0.13552362451508296,"w":0.73511291503906251,"t":"allows more energy to be delivered to the muscles and brain. This increase of"},{"y":0.86241985120423226,"c":1,"h":0.018644618144077585,"x":0.13749249673995639,"t":"blood and decrease of pressure in the blood vessels has been consistently related","w":0.77428288777669274},{"w":0.77629155476888023,"x":0.13545550298832079,"y":0.88063660697640178,"t":"to superior sport performance in everything from cricket batting, to golf putting and","c":1,"h":0.019461954167458884},{"x":0.088295688630921701,"t":"44","c":1,"y":0.92151162805026332,"h":0.014534883302221635,"w":0.026694043477376306},{"h":0.05140384010157395,"w":0.45230626424153653,"c":1,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","x":0.51802456464946445,"y":0.93670590176639579}],"w":2400,"h":3390}